  "description": "The hash premise. SHA-256 is FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 on every input length. Wherever this package names SHA-256 (the crypto digest a chain or a DAG is minted under, every digest a conformance vector records as SHA-256) it is SHA-256 over bytes, and a host whose digest differs on an input reproduces none of those there. Each vector gives `input`, a byte string as `hex` (lower case) repeated `repeat` times, and `sha256`, its digest as 64 lower-case hex digits; the export has checked every digest against the platform's own SHA-256. The lengths sit on the padding boundaries (55, 56, 57, 63, 64, 65, 119 and 120 bytes), beside the FIPS 180-4 messages, every byte value, and a million `a`.",
